#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:3
msgid "How to Migrate from PyCharm to Zed"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:5
msgid ""
"This guide covers how to set up Zed if you're coming from PyCharm, including "
"keybindings, settings, and the differences you should expect."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:7
msgid "Install Zed"
msgstr "安裝 Zed"

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:9
msgid "Zed is available on macOS, Windows, and Linux."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:11
msgid ""
"For macOS, you can download it from zed.dev/download, or install via "
"Homebrew:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:17
msgid ""
"For Windows, download the installer from zed.dev/download, or install via "
"winget:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:23
msgid ""
"For most Linux users, the easiest way to install Zed is through our "
"installation script:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:29
msgid ""
"After installation, you can launch Zed from your Applications folder "
"(macOS), Start menu (Windows), or directly from the terminal using: `zed .` "
"This opens the current directory in Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:33
msgid "Set Up the JetBrains Keymap"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:35
msgid ""
"If you're coming from PyCharm, the fastest way to feel at home is to use the "
"JetBrains keymap. During onboarding, you can select it as your base keymap. "
"If you missed that step, you can change it anytime:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:37 src/migrate/pycharm.md:357
msgid "Open Settings with `Cmd+,` (macOS) or `Ctrl+,` (Linux/Windows)"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:38
msgid "Search for `Base Keymap`"
msgstr "搜尋 `Base Keymap`"

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:39
msgid "Select `JetBrains`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:41
msgid ""
"This maps familiar shortcuts like `Shift Shift` for Search Everywhere, "
"`Cmd+O` for Go to Class, and `Cmd+Shift+A` for Find Action."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:43
msgid "Set Up Editor Preferences"
msgstr "設定編輯器偏好設定"

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:45
msgid ""
"You can configure most settings in the Settings Editor (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-,\\|ctrl-,</kbd>). For advanced settings, run `zed: "
"open settings file` from the Command Palette to edit your settings file "
"directly."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:47
msgid "Settings PyCharm users typically configure first:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:49
msgid "Zed Setting"
msgstr "Zed 設定"

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:49
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:51
msgid "`format_on_save`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:51
msgid "Auto-format when saving. Set to `\"on\"` to enable."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:52
msgid "`soft_wrap`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:52
msgid ""
"Wrap long lines. Options: `\"none\"`, `\"editor_width\"`, "
"`\"preferred_line_length\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:53
msgid "`preferred_line_length`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:53
msgid ""
"Column width for wrapping and rulers. Default is 80, PEP 8 recommends 79."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:54
msgid "`inlay_hints`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:54
msgid "Show parameter names and type hints inline, like PyCharm's hints."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:55
msgid "`relative_line_numbers`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:55
msgid "Useful if you're coming from IdeaVim."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:57
msgid ""
"Zed also supports per-project settings. Create a `.zed/settings.json` file "
"in your project root to override global settings for that project, similar "
"to how you might use `.idea` folders in PyCharm."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:59
msgid ""
"**Tip:** If you're joining an existing project, check `format_on_save` "
"before making your first commit. Otherwise you might accidentally reformat "
"an entire file when you only meant to change one line."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:61
msgid "Open or Create a Project"
msgstr "開啟或建立專案"

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:63
msgid ""
"After setup, press `Cmd+Shift+O` (with JetBrains keymap) to open a folder. "
"This becomes your workspace in Zed. Unlike PyCharm, there's no project "
"configuration wizard, no interpreter selection dialog, and no project "
"structure setup required."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:65
msgid ""
"To start a new project, create a directory using your terminal or file "
"manager, then open it in Zed. The editor will treat that folder as the root "
"of your project."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:67
msgid ""
"You can also launch Zed from the terminal inside any folder with: `zed .`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:70
msgid "Once inside a project:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:72
msgid ""
"Use `Cmd+Shift+O` or `Cmd+E` to jump between files quickly (like PyCharm's "
"\"Recent Files\")"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:73
msgid ""
"Use `Cmd+Shift+A` or `Shift Shift` to open the Command Palette (like "
"PyCharm's \"Search Everywhere\")"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:74
msgid "Use `Cmd+O` to search for symbols (like PyCharm's \"Go to Symbol\")"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:76
msgid ""
"Open buffers appear as tabs across the top. The Project Panel shows your "
"file tree and Git status. Toggle it with `Cmd+1` (just like PyCharm's "
"Project tool window)."
msgstr ""

