#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:224 src/migrate/pycharm.md:283
#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:289
msgid "\"label\""
msgstr "\"label\""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:216 src/migrate/pycharm.md:293
msgid "\"run\""
msgstr "\"run\""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:217 src/migrate/pycharm.md:221
#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:225
msgid "\"command\""
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:217
msgid "\"python main.py\""
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:220
msgid "\"test\""
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:221
msgid "\"pytest\""
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:224
msgid "\"test current file\""
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:225
msgid "\"pytest $ZED_FILE\""
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:230
msgid "Use `Ctrl+Alt+R` to run tasks quickly"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:231
msgid "Lean on your terminal (`Alt+F12`) for anything tasks don't cover"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:233
msgid "No Framework Integration"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:235
msgid ""
"PyCharm Professional's value for web development comes largely from its "
"framework integration. Django templates are understood and navigable. Flask "
"routes are indexed. SQLAlchemy models get special treatment. Template "
"variables autocomplete."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:237
msgid ""
"Zed has none of this. The language server sees Python code as Python code—it "
"doesn't understand that `@app.route` defines an endpoint or that a Django "
"model class creates database tables."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:241
msgid ""
"Use grep and file search liberally. `Cmd+Shift+F` with a regex can find "
"route definitions, model classes, or template usages."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:242
msgid ""
"Rely on your language server's \"find references\" (`Alt+F7`) for navigation—"
"it works, just without framework context"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:243
msgid ""
"Consider using framework-specific CLI tools (`python manage.py`, `flask "
"routes`) from Zed's terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:245
msgid ""
"**Tip:** For database work, pick up a dedicated tool like DataGrip, DBeaver, "
"or TablePlus. Many developers who switch to Zed keep DataGrip around "
"specifically for SQL."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:247
msgid "Tool Windows vs. Docks"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:249
msgid ""
"PyCharm organizes auxiliary views into numbered tool windows (Project = 1, "
"Python Console = 4, Terminal = Alt+F12, etc.). Zed uses a similar concept "
"called \"docks\":"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:251
msgid "PyCharm Tool Window"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:251
msgid "Zed Equivalent"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:251
msgid "Shortcut (JetBrains keymap)"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/pycharm.md:253
msgid "Project (1)"
msgstr "專案 (1)"

